                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Scribble</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Scribble</item>
                    <item name="Size" type_name="gh_single" type_code="5">25</item>
                    <item name="Text" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">This example model describes the minimal setup to make a single object in the ShapeDiver viewer transformable using a Gumball.

Important points to pay attention to:
* Use a named glTF 2.0 Display component
* Inject a name attribute in the object
* Match the name filter of the Gumball to the component and object's name.
* Test the presence of a transformation and send the Identity if none are present.
* Do not apply the transformation directly, but instead store it as an attribute.</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="1">
                    <chunk name="Attributes">
                      <items count="2">
                        <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
                          <X>18.05928</X>
                          <Y>24.20842</Y>
                          <W>1543.984</W>
                          <H>232.0093</H>
                        </item>
                        <item name="Pivot" type_name="gh_drawing_pointf" type_code="31">
                          <X>23.05928</X>
                          <Y>29.20842</Y>
                        </item>
                      </items>
                    </chunk>
                  </chunks>
                </chunk>
              </chunks>
            </chunk>
